    "notes": [
      "2D/100% initial concealed hand has a complete Reveal my hand button and full bottom actions. Revealed/selected hand uses horizontal scrolling: three cards are fully shown and a fourth clips; the persistent claim/turn context remains, while the larger Star heading clips at the top of the scrolled area.",
      "Cover and resumed-concealed originals remove private faces, rank labels and selection. The exercised Home frame shows Android Launcher, and Recents has an opaque dark preview with no private game content; these are runtime privacy captures, distinct from excluded pre-install Launcher evidence.",
      "Both 2D/100% after-play and public-outcome frames show Moxie catching Ari's Star claim with a public Moon; Ari uses light 1 and stays in. The named consequence and complete Deal the next round action are visible; lower seats extend beyond the scroll viewport.",
      "2D/100% next-round capture has already advanced to a round-2 public bluff result; the after-challenge capture is the round-4 public result. Both show complete named consequences and full Deal the next round actions.",
      "The 2D/100% winner is Orbit at round 14. A public Moon disproves Moxie's Crown claim, light 4 burns Moxie out, and the complete Return to lobby action is visible. The bottom seat rows remain scroll content.",
      "Match return, fresh scene Exit and fresh native Close each restore the full chooser with both presentation buttons. Fresh entries conceal all private faces and show complete Reveal controls; the final diagnostic is the chooser.",
      "The 2D/100% pre-install Launcher frame is infrastructure evidence and remains excluded, while the separate exercised Home frame remains a runtime privacy original.",
      "2D/200% initial concealed frame has a complete Reveal my hand button. Choose cards is visible, while the lower challenge action extends below the current viewport.",
